1. Overview
While the UI/UX design team finalises the high-fidelity mockups for the CyberVast Learning Management System (LMS), this sprint keeps the frontend team productive and directly invested in the LMS project. Rather than working on isolated exercises, interns will build the actual reusable component library and foundational scaffolding the LMS will rely on — work that feeds directly into the main project the moment hi-fi designs are delivered.

Why This Matters
•	Eliminates rework — components built to the design system will slot into the LMS without rebuilding.
•	Gives interns real ownership of production-bound code.
•	Shortens the integration window once hi-fi is handed off.
•	Builds intern familiarity with the CyberVast tech stack before the main sprint begins.

2. Sprint Objectives
By the end of this sprint, interns must deliver:

1.	A structured component library scaffold following an agreed folder and naming convention.
2.	A set of core UI components fully functional in isolation and documented.
3.	A design token file (CSS variables / Tailwind config) encoding the CyberVast brand palette.
4.	A living style guide or Storybook page showcasing all completed components.
5.	A brief technical handoff note ready to share with the UI/UX team.

