4. Tech Stack & Standards
Required Stack
•	React 18+ (functional components only — no class components)
•	Vite or Next.js 14+ as the build/framework layer
•	Tailwind CSS for styling (utility-first; no plain CSS unless unavoidable)
•	TypeScript preferred; JavaScript with JSDoc type hints acceptable
•	ESLint + Prettier configured and enforced

Component Standards
•	Every component lives in src/components/<ComponentName>/<ComponentName>.tsx
•	Co-located test file: <ComponentName>.test.tsx (Vitest or Jest)
•	Props typed via TypeScript interface or PropTypes
•	No inline styles — all styling via Tailwind classes or CSS tokens
•	ARIA attributes included on all interactive elements
•	Components must be responsive — mobile-first breakpoints

Git Workflow
•	Branch naming: feat/component-name (e.g. feat/button-component)
•	Commit messages follow Conventional Commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:
•	A pull request is raised for each component — no direct pushes to main
•	PR description must include: what was built, how to run it, screenshot or gif

