6. Submission & Review Process
During the Sprint
•	Daily stand-up (async or live): share what you built yesterday, what you're building today, any blockers.
•	Each component PR must be reviewed and merged before moving to the next P0 item.
•	Use the team's shared channel to post screenshots of components as they're completed.

End-of-Sprint Submission
•	GitHub repo link shared with the team lead — all PRs merged, main branch clean.
•	Style guide / Storybook deployed to a preview URL (Vercel, Netlify, or GitHub Pages).
•	Technical handoff note (1 page max) covering: stack decisions, known limitations, open questions for the UI/UX team.

Review Criteria
•	Code Quality: Clean, readable, typed, follows agreed conventions.
•	Component Accuracy: Variants and states match the component spec above.
•	Accessibility: Keyboard navigable, ARIA labelled, passes basic a11y audit.
•	Responsiveness: Works across mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports.
•	Documentation: Style guide is clear; PR descriptions are complete.

