8. Important Notes
This is real work, not a drill. The components you build here will be reviewed for inclusion in the CyberVast LMS codebase. Treat every PR as if it is going to production — because it might.

•	If a component spec feels ambiguous, make a reasonable assumption, document it in the PR, and flag it — don't block.
•	You are free to propose improvements to any component spec; raise them in the team channel before implementing.
•	P2 items are only for interns who complete P0 and P1 early — do not skip P0/P1 items to work on P2.
•	Quality over quantity. Two excellent, fully tested components beat five half-finished ones.


